{
 "_source": "Two live plants, 2026-11-19, local time (UTC+2). Bus 1: a BTicino 3550 99-zone central unit (#0) running zones 3 and 4, and zone 2, a standalone thermostat with a fan coil (actuator 2#1) the 3550 does not run, cooling at 22.0 with 23.5 measured, reached through an F461 2.0.11 and an F455 1.0.76. Bus 2: 34 standalone thermostats, no central unit, reached through a MyHomeServer1 3.87.13 and a 3488 3.2.5 (set up under the model name MyHomeServer1). Each trace is the WHO 4 frames of one Home Assistant instance's debug log in a time window: tx a frame it sent (logged when the gateway acknowledged it), rx a frame it received on its event session or as a reply. No address, MAC or name of either plant.",
 "_traces": {
  "f461_zone2_off_8s": "F461 Home Assistant instance, before the change. Another client switched zone 2 off and, 8.3 s later, on again. The fan coil reported its off 3.1 s after the zone's and its on 4.9 s after the zone was running again.",
  "f461_zone2_off_1s": "F461 Home Assistant instance, before the change. Zone 2 switched off through this instance and on again 1.2 s later through the F455's. No actuator frame of zone 2 follows; the zone was shown idle. At 16:30:52 another client asked every actuator (its request is not on this event session): the fan coil answers 8, fan speed 3, as before the off.",
  "f461_zone2_off_2s_asked": "F461 Home Assistant instance, with the change. Zone 2 switched off and, 2.0 s later, on again through this instance. It asks every actuator once the zone runs and the fan coil answers 8.",
  "f455_zone2_off_2s_asked": "The F455 Home Assistant instance during the same two seconds: it sees the F461's frames and the fan coil's answer, and asks as well once its bus is quiet.",
  "myhomeserver1_zone53_off_2s_asked": "MyHomeServer1 Home Assistant instance, with the change. Zone 53 (a plain heating valve, open) switched off and on again 2.3 s later through this instance. The valve's state comes at 16:53:43.446, 0.16 s before the 3488 instance logs its request for every actuator as acknowledged, and again after this instance's own request (acknowledged at 16:53:46.609).",
  "g3488_zone53_off_2s_asked": "The 3488 Home Assistant instance during the same seconds; its request for every actuator is logged as acknowledged at 16:53:43.608.",
  "f461_zone2_off_2s_actuator_reported": "F461 Home Assistant instance, zone 2 found on the bus, off for 2.5 s. This time the fan coil reported its off (5) 2.1 s after the zone's, before the zone was on again, and its on (8) 5.6 s after the zone's on. Taken with a first version of the change, which asked every actuator here as well (the tx row at 17:03:24.085, answered 5); the rule does not ask for an actuator that has reported."
 },
